# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single source of control for all HTB lab folders under easy/.
# Policy: track ONLY the written deliverables (the Markdown writeups).
# Everything else — recon evidence, loot, private keys, PoC exploits, tooling,
# PDFs/HTML, pcaps, screenshots — is ignored and never leaves this machine.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything by default.
*

# 2) …but let git descend into subdirectories so it can find the files below.
!*/

# 3) Whitelist the deliverable docs (these names are kept at any depth).
!GLOBAL_CONTEXT.md
!WALKTHROUGH.md
!walkthrough.md
!REPORT.md
!STORY.md
!CTF_GUIDE.md

# 4) Keep this control file itself (root only).
!/.gitignore

# ── Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • To also publish a lab's tooling or evidence, add a targeted exception, e.g.:
#       !cohort/00try/ws_exec.py
#   (place it AFTER the rules above so it wins).
# • HTB flags in the tracked Markdown are redacted to [REDACTED-HTB-FLAG].
#   Credentials/passwords in the writeups are NOT redacted — review before
#   making the repo public, and confirm each machine is retired per HTB rules.
